    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense enters May 11th facing a mixed bag of matchups, with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the daily board as our clear-cut priority. Despite a potential disadvantage against Ryan Weathers\u2019 lefty profile, **Gunnar Henderson** earns an elite 63.77 rating; the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and the high probability of an aggressive approach against a slow-delivering pitcher makes him our primary target for stolen base upside. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** (61.69) benefits from a high-leverage opportunity against Roki Sasaki. While Sasaki is a formidable talent, his projected xERA of 5.30 suggests a vulnerability that **Heliot Ramos** is positioned to exploit from the heart of the order, providing the best ceiling among our outfielders today.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the margins, where **Josh Jung** (46.79) narrowly missed the final lineup spot behind **Nolan Schanuel** (47.75). While **Josh Jung** offers respectable pop against Michael Soroka, the optimizer favored **Nolan Schanuel**\u2019s stability to preserve our remaining game caps, viewing the marginal difference in projected output as insufficient to trigger a start. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding the top of the order: **Andy Pages** (46.31) and **Kyle Tucker** (53.64) are forced into a tough matchup against the 2.60 xERA of Trevor McDonald. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also facing a difficult test in Drew Rasmussen, our offensive production relies heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos** to anchor the scoring in a day characterized by several high-end opposing starters. We continue to monitor the lineups for **Coby Mayo** and others, as any unexpected shifts in the batting order could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth.",
